// Bug 2.13: @exportblackwhite/@exportframe are each only genuinely
// implemented for one specific asset type: @exportblackwhite for a plain
// bitmap imported via the (now-removed) GUI's image-import dialog
// (LImageQImage::ExportBlackWhite), @exportframe for a level-editor asset
// (ImageLevelEditor::ExportFrame). Every other asset type - including
// every charset/sprite .flf actually bundled in this repo, like
// sample_sprite.flf - used to fall through to an empty-stub virtual
// method (LImage::ExportBlackWhite's `{}` base, CharsetImage::ExportFrame's
// dead stub that writes an empty QByteArray), so both directives compiled
// clean and silently wrote a zero-byte output file with no error at all.
//
// Fix direction chosen: since implementing real per-asset-type support
// for either directive is new functionality (not a bugfix), and
// @exportblackwhite's one working asset type is already unreachable from
// this GUI-less CLI-only fork (see KNOWN_BUGS.md), both handlers
// (Parser::HandleExportBW / Parser::HandleExportFrame, parser.cpp) now
// check the loaded asset's real type with a dynamic_cast before calling
// into it, and raise a clear ErrorHandler::e.Error(...) instead of
// silently writing empty output when the asset isn't the one type that
// actually works.
//
// This snippet covers @exportblackwhite specifically; see the companion
// 2_13_exportframe_wrong_asset_type.ras for @exportframe's own check
// (a single compile can only ever surface the first Error(), so the two
// directives need separate snippets for both fixes to get real
// regression coverage).
//
// Method B (compile-time), no VICE step. Pre-fix: compiles clean, writes
// a 0-byte 2_13_export_bw.bin. Post-fix: fails to compile with a clear
// "only implemented for a plain bitmap image" error.
program Bug_2_13_ExportBlackWhiteEmptyOutput;

@exportblackwhite "sample_sprite.flf" "2_13_export_bw.bin" 0 0 8 8

begin
	loop();
end.
